config AL_SERDES
	bool "Annapurna Labs 25G SerDes + 10GBASE-R PCS (UNVR SFP+ bring-up)"
	depends on OF_CONTROL
	help
	  Bring up the Annapurna Labs (AL-324 / Alpine V2) 25G SerDes lane for
	  the UNVR's 10G SFP+ port at a FIXED 10.3125 Gbps (10GBASE-R), with KR
	  auto-neg and link-training DISABLED. Adds the `serdes` command to run
	  the init and read lane status (PLL lock, signal-detect, CDR lock,
	  rx-valid, PCS block-lock). Base addresses come from the device tree.

	  This is the SerDes/PCS (PMA) half of 10G ethernet only; the MAC/UDMA
	  come from the al_eth driver. Compile-only — the lane bring-up needs
	  on-hardware iteration.
